      "name": "Step 1",
      "text": "Building an ADU is an exciting journey, and knowing what to expect during construction can make the whole process much smoother. Once your permits are in hand, the real work begins! You'll typically start with site preparation, which involves clearing the area and laying the foundation. This sets the stage for the entire structure, so precision here is crucial. After that, the framing goes up, quickly giving you a visual sense of the ADU's footprint and layout."
